#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""A persistent ACL2 session on bb2 over a lane's remote tree, driven from the Mac.

The lanes' inner loop was a bb2 certify of 20-45 minutes; the Mac REPL refuses
bb2 certificates (their system-book hashes differ), so seats hand-rolled an `ld`
on bb2 over the certified closure.  This is that, supported:

    tools/bb2_repl start books/cns.lisp            # sync, include the book's includes, wait
    tools/bb2_repl load cns                        # ld the book's events; EVERY error with its form
    tools/bb2_repl load cns --skip-proofs          # the same without proofs: generator errors in seconds
    tools/bb2_repl load cns --until fn2-x            # the prefix; then, after an edit:
    tools/bb2_repl load cns --from fn2-x --through fn2-y   # --from keeps the session's world
    tools/bb2_repl send cns '(pe (quote fn2-cns-step))'
    tools/bb2_repl status cns | list | stop cns

The session lives in bb2:~/fn2-<lane>/ (the lane is this worktree's name under
build/lanes/, else `--lane`).  `start` rsyncs this worktree there first, exactly as
tools/box_certify_bb2.sh does (content-compared, so unchanged files keep their
remote mtimes and certificates), unless the lane is not this worktree's (the
deputy's ~/fn2-main is never written from a lane) or `--no-sync`.  It then runs a
server under swarm-build (SWARM_MEM_MAX, default 12G), detached with `nohup
setsid`; the server writes its own PID to build/bb2-repl/NAME/server.pid on bb2
and stops itself after `--idle` minutes without a request (default 60).

The warm-up sends the book's own top-level `include-book` forms (its certified
closure, from the certificates in the remote tree; a dependency whose source no
longer matches its certificate is included uncertified, and `status` names it),
then `(deflabel bb2-repl-base)`.  `load` undoes the world back to that label
(`ubt!`), syncs, and sends every top-level form of the book (or the range) one at a
time, continuing past refusals, and prints each refused form with its first error;
a refusal whose error names an event refused earlier in the same load is marked
"follow-on".  The whole output of the load is kept on bb2 and its path printed.

After an edit to a book the session INCLUDES (a dependency, not the book it loads),
stop and start it: the warm-up re-includes, and a dependency whose source no longer
matches its certificate is loaded from source with its proofs skipped (measured: a
changed books/machines.lisp under tests/machine-arms-unit.lisp, warm-up 3.5 s), so
the edited generator runs at once; `load` then checks the book above it with proofs.

A green here means ACL2 admitted the forms in a session over the remote tree's
certificates (with `--skip-proofs`, only that they translate and expand).  It is
not a certificate: certify with tools/box_certify_bb2.sh.

Never kill by pattern: `stop` asks the server; if it does not answer, the client
signals the PID in server.pid only after checking that /proc/PID/cmdline is this
session's `bb2_repl serve NAME`.
"""
